{
  "_how_this_works": [
    "A patch is a list of segments played one after another. Each segment is one oscillator sweeping from f0 to f1 (Hz) over ms milliseconds.",
    "wave: sine, square, saw, triangle, noise (f sets how fast the noise changes) or silence. vol: 0-255. atk / rel: fade in / out in ms (rel up to 1020).",
    "vib / depth: vibrato rate in Hz and depth 0-255. loop: true makes a patch repeat as the tag's background sound.",
    "A profile maps each play event to [patch, animation]. `extends` copies another profile first, so a new profile only lists what differs.",
    "Events: place remove shake swing tilt_l tilt_r roll impact throw red green blue hit damaged destroyed ambient clap.",
    "Animations: off solid breathe flash chase sparkle rainbow alternate halves fade.",
    "All sounds here are original and generated by the brick's own synthesiser. None are recordings."
  ],
